  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 AM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nA cold front is currently moving through bringing with it some\nof the coldest temperatures we have yet to see this Fall. With\nthe cold airmass and limited cloud cover at night, highs will \nonly reach the 50s and lows will drop down to the low to mid\n30s today and through the weekend. This has prompted the\nissuance of a Freeze Warning for portions of the Ozark \nFoothills in southeast Missouri and southern and southwestern \nIllinois, and a Frost Advisory for southern Indiana and western \nKentucky for tonight. Temperatures will drop further Saturday \nnight, prompting the issuance of a Freeze Watch for the entire \nregion that will end the growing season for the year.\n\nMonday, high pressure will settle in place bringing continued \ndry conditions, southerly winds, and another warm-up back into \nthe 60s across the region. These conditions should persist \nthrough at least mid-week. Models suggest another positively \ntilted trough may pass through Wednesday evening/Thursday \nmorning that may bring a few sprinkles, but confidence is low at\nthe moment.",
